      "node_id": "kg_doc_6",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Unbeaten Tracks in Japan (日本奥地紀行 , Nihon Okuchi Kikō ) is a travel diary written by Isabella Bird of her trip to Japan in 1878, at the age of 47. It was first published in English in 1881 by G. P. Putnam's Sons. It was later translated into Japanese by Tsurukichi Itō.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
